  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "This paper compares the post-sample performance of peer-reviewed predictors with data-mined benchmarks.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   2
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 2,
  "citation": "To data mine, we search 29,000 accounting ratios for statistical evidence of predictive power.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   2
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 3,
  "citation": "These categorizations are made manually, by reading the papers.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   3
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 3,
  "citation": "We find similar results controlling for CAPM and Fama-French 3 (FF3) + momentum exposure, among many other controls.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   3
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 4,
  "citation": "should be shrunk toward the average of about zero to account for multiple comparisons",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   4,
   20
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 6,
  "citation": "Yan and Zheng reject the null of no predictability based on both bootstrap and out-of-sample tests.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   6
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 6,
  "citation": "Following up on our paper, Chen and Dim (2025) and Marrow and Nagel (2024) use empirical Bayes to mine data more rigorously.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   6
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 7,
  "citation": "We then generate 29,315 accounting ratios (signals) using two functional forms",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   7
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 7,
  "citation": "This procedure aims to be the simplest possible data mining benchmark for peer-reviewed predictors.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   7
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 7,
  "citation": "A more sophisticated selection would filter on data availability in real time.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   7
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 8,
  "citation": "Each June, we sort the 29,000 accounting ratios into five bins based on their mean long-short returns over the past 30 years (in-sample) and compute the mean return over the next year within each bin (out-of-sample).",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   8
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 12,
  "citation": "Peer-reviewed predictors come from the October 2024 release of the Chen and Zimmermann (2022) (CZ) dataset.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   12
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 12,
  "citation": "This dataset is built from 212 firm-level variables that were shown to predict returns cross-sectionally in academic journals.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   12
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 12,
  "citation": "The CZ data is a uniquely accurate representation of the literature: unlike other large-scale replications, CZ show that their t-stats are generally a good match for the t-stats in the original papers.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   12
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 12,
  "citation": "We keep only predictors that produce mean long-short return t-stats > 2.0 in the original samples.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   12
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 12,
  "citation": "For each of these published strategies, we construct a data-mined benchmark by applying the same statistical treatment to the 29,000 accounting ratios.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   12
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 13,
  "citation": "filter for t-stats > 2.0, sign and normalize to have +100 bps mean return in the original samples.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   13
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 13,
  "citation": "on average, this process selects roughly 6,000 data-mined strategies for each published predictor.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   13
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 13,
  "citation": "This result suggests that peer-reviewed research provides limited additional information about post-sample performance compared to data mining.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   13
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 13,
  "citation": "The sample s is either the original sample or the post-sample period.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   13
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 13,
  "citation": "This separation ensures our t-stat filters do not produce look-ahead bias",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   13
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 14,
  "citation": "Shaded area shows one standard error for the published predictors, clustered by calendar month and predictor.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   14,
   45
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 15,
  "citation": "This method avoids look-ahead bias and is arguably the most straightforward way to mine data.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   15
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 15,
  "citation": "This result is consistent with false discovery controls, which typically depend on the distribution of test statistics rather than the number of tests",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   15
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 16,
  "citation": "We apply these classifications based on manual reading of the original papers.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   16
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 16,
  "citation": "incremental to, and more pronounced than previously documented earnings-related anomalies.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   16
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 19,
  "citation": "‘Versus Data Mining’ is ‘Post-Sample’ minus the performance of data-mined benchmarks.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   19,
   21
  ]
 },
 {
  "piece": "CLZ",
  "pdf": "docs/sources/pdf/lecture-o4-v3/arxiv-2212.10317/2212.10317v7.pdf",
  "empreinte": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "page": 19,
  "citation": "Standard errors (parentheses) are clustered by calendar month and predictor.",
  "sha256_pdf_recalcule": "e8f061ef05e4449475ee4dbd8924e6f971f372969112dbb39f8f1cb716bbc89a",
  "empreinte_conforme": true,
  "trouvee_sur_la_page": true,
  "pages_ou_trouvee": [
   19,
